get.description:
SSE endpoint for real-time blockchain events on a specific trade.

Listens to:
- trade_created
- trade_accepted
- deposit_paid
- step_verified
- step_completed
- trade_completed
- kyc_verified
- proof_of_funds_verified
- document_issued
- lc_issued
- lc_paid

Usage:
    const eventSource = new EventSource(
        '/api/commodity/trades/{trade_id}/events/stream',
        { withCredentials: true }
    );
    eventSource.onmessage = (event) => {
        const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
        console.log('Trade event:', data);
    };

post.description:
Allocate multiple providers to pay a supplier for a subscription.
Supports syndicated financing where multiple funders contribute.

Example:
{
    "supplier_order_id": 123,
    "allocations": [
        {"provider_id": 1, "percentage": 60.0},
        {"provider_id": 2, "percentage": 40.0}
    ]
}
